.TH XmLoadTheme 3X "Motif 2.3.8 modernization"
.SH NAME
XmLoadTheme \(em merge a named theme profile and re-apply appearance
resources to a widget subtree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/Xm\&.h>
\fBvoid \fBXmLoadTheme\fP\fR(
\fBWidget \fBshell\fR\fR,
\fBconst char *\fBname\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBXmLoadTheme\fP loads a theme profile named \fIname\fP and merges it
into the resource database of the screen that \fIshell\fP lives on\&.
The theme profile is an ordinary Xrm resource file\&.  The function
searches, in order:
.IP "  1." 3
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/motif/themes/\fIname\fB\fR (or
\fB$HOME/.config/motif/themes/\fIname\fB\fR when
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fP is unset)
.IP "  2." 3
each directory in \fB$XDG_DATA_DIRS\fR (default \fB/usr/share\fR), as
\fB<dir>/motif/themes/\fIname\fB\fR
.LP
A \fIname\fP containing a \fB/\fP is used as a direct file path\&.
.PP
After merging, the theme's palette key (the \fB*background\fP resource)
is applied: every Manager, Primitive and Gadget under \fIshell\fP has
its background updated and the foreground, select and shadow colors are
recalculated through the color-calculation procedure (see
\fBXmSetColorCalculation(3)\fP and \fBXmChangeColor(3)\fP)\&.  Other
resources in the theme file take effect for widgets created
afterwards\&.
.PP
Applications can be themed without code changes by setting the
\fBMOTIF_THEME\fP environment variable to a theme name; it is applied
at the first vendor shell realize\&.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "\fIshell\fP" 10
Specifies the shell whose subtree is re-applied
.IP "\fIname\fP" 10
Specifies the theme profile name (or a file path)
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.nf
/* explicit control */
XmLoadTheme (toplevel, "high-contrast");

/* zero-code-change alternative */
setenv ("MOTIF_THEME", "high-contrast", 1);
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP "\fBMOTIF_THEME\fP" 10
Theme profile applied at the first vendor shell realize (zero
application code changes)\&.
.IP "\fBMOTIF_SCALE\fP" 10
Display scale factor in permille (e.g. 2000 = 2x); consumed by the
\fBXmScreen\fP resource \fBXmNscaleFactor\fP (see
\fBXmScreen(3)\fP)\&.
.IP "\fBMOTIF_A11Y_LOG\fP" 10
When set to a writable file path, the accessibility bridge skeleton
reports every widget creation (name, class, role, geometry) to that
file as JSON lines\&.  Unset means no accessibility reporting and no
behavior change\&.
.SH FILES
.IP "  \(bu" 3
themes/default, themes/high\-contrast, themes/monochrome\-legacy
(in the source tree) are the shipped example profiles
.SH ERRORS
.PP
If the theme profile cannot be found or parsed, a warning is issued
through \fBXmeWarning(3)\fP and the widget tree is left unchanged\&.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
XmChangeColor(3), XmGetColorCalculation(3), XmRenderTable(3)
